If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy and a long-term-opioid-reassessment-schedule has a reassessment-interval and the reassessment-interval includes at most 3 months then every clinician should use the long-term-opioid-reassessment-schedule for the patient.
If a clinician sees a new-patient and the new-patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy and a long-term-opioid-reassessment-schedule has a reassessment-interval and the reassessment-interval includes at most 3 months then the clinician should use the long-term-opioid-reassessment-schedule for the new-patient.
